# INTensity then LOG at the focal plane of the far-field Cassegrain (cmdref: Diffraction / Outputs)
# INT propagates the wavefront to the element (the far-field leg of this deck) and prints
# the peak; LOG redisplays the SAME intensity as log10 (no new propagation) -- it is the
# log10-intensity DISPLAY, not transcript logging (that is JOUrnal).  The /null lines
# answer the plot-device prompt the first plot of a session asks.
# MODEL: 256
# DEADLINE: 120
old $RES/pymacos/tests/Rx/Rx_Cass_FarField.in
int 6
/null
log 6
# EXPECT: Tracing rays past\s+6 elements
# EXPECT: Peak intensity= 3\.2881\d+D\+05; Peak occurs at i=\s*129, j=\s*129
# EXPECT: (Peak intensity=[\s\S]*){2}
# EXPECT-NOT: No data to display
# EXPECT-NOT: Too few rays
